From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] setup: guard parasail_ssw_profile() against a NULL
 profile

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; the real fix is a NULL check at the top of parasail_ssw_profile() in jeffdaily/parasail's src/pssw.c]

parasail's profile creators have no scalar fallback by design: with no
SIMD ISA, parasail_profile_create_8/16() return NULL ("caller must check
for non-NULL profile"), and so does parasail_ssw_init(). But
parasail_ssw_profile() reads profile->s1 and profile->matrix before any
check, and parasail_ssw() passes it parasail_ssw_init()'s result
unchecked, so on riscv64 both parasail.ssw_profile() and plain
parasail.ssw() die with SIGSEGV. That is the exit-139 crash in
test_ssw (the 'blosum62' set_value message printed just before it
comes from the previous test, test_matrix, which passes).

It is not related to the cpuid stub: on riscv64 configure reports no
SIMD ISA, so HAVE_SSE2/AVX2/NEON/ALTIVEC are all 0 and the dispatchers
never call parasail_can_use_*() at all.

Initialise s1/matrix only when profile is non-NULL and return NULL via
the library's own PARASAIL_CHECK_NULL() otherwise, so ssw()/ssw_profile()
return None in Python instead of crashing the interpreter.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 setup.py | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/setup.py b/setup.py
index a2c6b40..7cf8f4e 100644
--- a/setup.py
+++ b/setup.py
@@ -362,6 +362,25 @@ def build_parasail(libname):
         with open(dispatch_c, 'w') as f:
             f.write(fallback_re.sub(scalar_fallback, dispatch_src))
 
+    # Profile creation has no scalar fallback, so with no SIMD ISA
+    # parasail_ssw_init() returns NULL; parasail_ssw_profile() (and so
+    # parasail_ssw()) then dereferences it and segfaults. Return NULL instead.
+    pssw_c = os.path.join(parasail_root, 'src', 'pssw.c')
+    with open(pssw_c) as f:
+        pssw_src = f.read()
+    pssw_deref = ('    const char *s1 = profile->s1;\n'
+                  '    const parasail_matrix_t *matrix = profile->matrix;\n')
+    pssw_anchor = ('    /* find the end loc first with the faster implementation */\n'
+                   '    has8 =')
+    if pssw_deref in pssw_src and pssw_anchor in pssw_src:
+        pssw_src = pssw_src.replace(pssw_deref,
+            '    const char *s1 = profile ? profile->s1 : NULL;\n'
+            '    const parasail_matrix_t *matrix = profile ? profile->matrix : NULL;\n', 1)
+        pssw_src = pssw_src.replace(pssw_anchor,
+            '    PARASAIL_CHECK_NULL(profile);\n\n' + pssw_anchor, 1)
+        with open(pssw_c, 'w') as f:
+            f.write(pssw_src)
+
     root = find_file('configure', parasail_root)
     if root is None:
         print("Unable to find parasail configure script")
